#set page(paper: "a4", numbering: "1")
#set text(font: "Courier", size: 12pt)
#set par(justify: true)

#let scene(title) = [
  #v(1.5em)
  *#upper(title)*
  #v(0.5em)
]

#let character(name) = [
  #v(0.5em)
  #align(center)[*#upper(name)*]
]

#let dialogue(text) = [
  #pad(left: 1.5in, right: 1in)[#text]
]

#let parenthetical(text) = [
  #pad(left: 1.5in, right: 1in)[_(#text)_]
]

#let action(text) = [
  #v(0.5em)
  #text
]

#align(center)[
  = TEACH YOU A LESSON (참교육)
  \
  *Episode 1: The Death of Authority*
  \
  Written for Television
]

#scene("EXT. JINWON HIGH SCHOOL - DAY - ESTABLISHING")
#action([
The campus of Jinwon High School looks pristine from the outside. Sunlit brick, manicured lawns, a large banner reading: "NURTURING THE LEADERS OF TOMORROW." 

But as the CAMERA PUSHES IN toward the third-floor windows, the illusion shatters. The muffled sounds of screaming, crashing desks, and cruel laughter bleed through the glass. It sounds less like a place of learning and more like a prison riot.
])

#scene("INT. JINWON HIGH SCHOOL - HALLWAY - CONTINUOUS")
#action([
Students run through the halls, chasing each other. A boy is shoved into a row of lockers. Teachers walk by, eyes glued to the floor, actively ignoring the violence. Survival here means looking the other way.
])

#scene("INT. JINWON HIGH SCHOOL - CLASSROOM 3-2 - CONTINUOUS")
#action([
Absolute anarchy. 

A group of students in the back are openly smoking, blowing clouds of grey smoke toward the ceiling. Others are playing mobile games, their phones blaring at maximum volume. 

In the center of the room, a frail, trembling student, JIN-WOO (18), is on his hands and knees. He is picking up pieces of a torn textbook. 

Sitting in the front row, with his muddy sneakers propped up on the teacher's podium, is BAE DO-JIN (18). Do-jin is the apex predator of this school. Arrogant, untouchable, and protected by his parents' wealth and the youth protection laws. He tosses an empty juice box at Jin-woo's head.
])

#character("BAE DO-JIN")
#dialogue([
Hey, Jin-woo. If you don't tape every single page back together before the bell rings, I'm taking you to the bathroom during lunch. And you know how much you hate the bathroom.
])

#action([
Jin-woo flinches, tears welling in his eyes. He frantically scrambles to gather the ripped pages. 

At the front of the room stands MR. KIM (late 30s), a weary, exhausted homeroom teacher. His tie is loose, his posture defeated. He holds a piece of chalk, staring at the blackboard. He looks at Jin-woo, then at Do-jin. His hands shake.
])

#character("MR. KIM")
#parenthetical("voice barely a whisper")
#dialogue([
Do-jin... please. Leave him alone. Take your feet off the podium. We need to start the lesson.
])

#character("BAE DO-JIN")
#parenthetical("doesn't look up from his phone")
#dialogue([
I'm busy, Teach. Just write whatever you want. We're not looking anyway.
])

#action([
The class snickers. Mr. Kim takes a trembling breath. He remembers why he became a teacher. He reaches out and gently taps Do-jin's foot.
])

#character("MR. KIM")
#dialogue([
I said, take them down. Now.
])

#action([
Do-jin stops his game. The class goes deathly quiet. Do-jin slowly lowers his feet, stands up, and steps right into Mr. Kim's personal space. He towers over the older man. The malice in Do-jin's eyes is genuinely terrifying.
])

#character("BAE DO-JIN")
#parenthetical("smiling menacingly")
#dialogue([
Did you just touch me? Are you hitting a student, Mr. Kim? Because my mom told me if a teacher ever lays a hand on me, I should report it to the police for child abuse.
])

#action([
Before Mr. Kim can respond, Do-jin aggressively shoves the teacher's shoulder. Mr. Kim stumbles back, dropping his chalk. It shatters on the floor.
])

#character("BAE DO-JIN")
#dialogue([
Pick it up. 
])

#action([
Mr. Kim stares at the shattered chalk. He looks around the room. Every student is either recording him on their phones or laughing. The teacher's authority is completely, utterly dead. 

Defeated, humiliated, Mr. Kim slowly bends down to pick up the chalk. Do-jin smirks and blows smoke over the teacher's bowed head.
])

#scene("INT. MINISTRY OF EDUCATION - ASSEMBLY HALL - DAY")
#action([
Camera flashes illuminate the grand hall. MINISTER CHOI GANG-SEOK (60s), a man with eyes like a hawk and a posture of iron, stands before a massive assembly of reporters, politicians, and educators. 

A giant screen behind him displays horrifying statistics: "TEACHER ASSAULTS UP 400%," "RECORD NUMBERS OF EDUCATOR RESIGNATIONS."
])

#character("MINISTER CHOI")
#dialogue([
Look at these numbers. Are we proud of this? A decade ago, we passed the Anti-Corporal Punishment laws to protect our children from abuse. It was a noble endeavor. A necessary one. But look at what it has mutated into!
])

#action([
Minister Choi slams his fist onto the podium. The microphone feedback screeches.
])

#character("MINISTER CHOI")
#dialogue([
The students know the teachers cannot touch them. They know the law is an impenetrable shield for their cruelty. The classroom has become a warzone where the educators are the victims! Where the good students are collateral damage! Today, the Ministry of Education says: No more.
])

#action([
ASSEMBLYMAN PARK (50s, slick, corrupt) stands up from the front row, grabbing a microphone.
])

#character("ASSEMBLYMAN PARK")
#dialogue([
Minister Choi, this rhetoric is dangerous! Are you suggesting we reverse the law? That we allow teachers to beat children again? The public will not stand for a regression of human rights!
])

#character("MINISTER CHOI")
#parenthetical("eyes narrowing")
#dialogue([
I am not suggesting regression, Assemblyman. I am suggesting specialized intervention. 
])

#action([
The screen behind him changes to a striking, imposing logo. A sword crossing a pen. A collective gasp echoes through the hall.
])

#character("MINISTER CHOI")
#dialogue([
Effective immediately, the National Assembly has passed the Special Act on the Protection of Educational Rights. Under this act, we are launching the Educational Rights Protection Bureau—the ERPB. They are not mere teachers. They are enforcers. They will be deployed to the most corrupted schools in this nation. And they will remind the monsters disguised as students what happens when you cross the line.
])

#scene("INT. ERPB HEADQUARTERS - BASEMENT LEVEL - DAY")
#action([
A state-of-the-art surveillance hub hidden deep beneath the Ministry. Server racks hum. Screens display CCTV feeds from hundreds of classrooms.

IM HAN-RIM (30s), a fiercely athletic former military operative, is reviewing the footage of Mr. Kim being humiliated by Do-jin. She crushes a paper cup of coffee in her fist, her jaw clenched in rage.

Minister Choi enters the room, followed by a man hidden in the shadows of the doorway.
])

#character("MINISTER CHOI")
#dialogue([
Jinwon High School. The teachers have entirely given up. The principal is taking bribes from the parents to cover up student crimes. It's ground zero for the collapse of educational authority.
])

#action([
The man in the shadows steps forward into the harsh fluorescent light. 

NA HWA-JIN (40s). He is tall, imposing, with a face carved from granite and eyes that look like they've seen the depths of hell. He wears a perfectly tailored, pitch-black suit. He exudes an aura of absolute, terrifying calm.
])

#character("NA HWA-JIN")
#dialogue([
Bae Do-jin. Eighteen. Multiple counts of extortion, assault, and harassment of faculty. Protected by the Juvenile Act and his father's construction empire. 
])

#character("MINISTER CHOI")
#dialogue([
He needs to be broken, Hwa-jin. The entire school needs to see that their shield is gone. The public will be watching. The media will try to tear you down. Can you do it?
])

#action([
Hwa-jin rolls his shoulders. He adjusts his cuffs. A predatory, almost sadistic smile crosses his face.
])

#character("NA HWA-JIN")
#dialogue([
Minister, I'm going to teach them a lesson they'll never forget.
])

#scene("EXT. JINWON HIGH SCHOOL - THE NEXT MORNING")
#action([
A sleek black government sedan pulls up to the front gates. The doors open. 

Hwa-jin steps out. He adjusts his tie, grabs a silver Ministry-issued baton from the passenger seat, and walks onto the campus. 

The aura around him is so intense, so overwhelmingly dominant, that students in the courtyard instinctively part ways. Conversations die in his wake. They stare at him in fear and confusion. He doesn't look like a teacher. He looks like a hitman.
])

#scene("INT. JINWON HIGH SCHOOL - STAFF ROOM - DAY")
#action([
The staff room is a depressing sight. Teachers sit in silence, grading papers like zombies. Mr. Kim is at his desk, staring blankly at a typed piece of paper. 

CLOSE UP: It's a resignation letter.

Suddenly, the staff room door opens. Hwa-jin enters. The room goes quiet. The VICE PRINCIPAL hurries over, sweating.
])

#character("VICE PRINCIPAL")
#dialogue([
Excuse me? Parents aren't allowed in the staff room during—
])

#action([
Hwa-jin flashes his ERPB badge. The Vice Principal freezes.
])

#character("NA HWA-JIN")
#dialogue([
I'm not a parent. I'm taking over Classroom 3-2. Mr. Kim, you're on paid administrative leave starting right now. Go home and sleep.
])

#character("MR. KIM")
#parenthetical("looking up, bewildered")
#dialogue([
But... Do-jin... you can't... he'll ruin you.
])

#character("NA HWA-JIN")
#parenthetical("softening just a fraction")
#dialogue([
You did your best, Mr. Kim. Let the adults handle it from here.
])

#scene("INT. JINWON HIGH SCHOOL - CLASSROOM 3-2 - DAY")
#action([
The classroom is in its usual state of chaos. Do-jin has a Bluetooth speaker blasting heavy metal music. He is throwing darts at the blackboard. Jin-woo is cowering in the corner.
])

#character("BAE DO-JIN")
#dialogue([
Where the hell is Kim? I wanted to see him cry again today!
])

#action([
*CRASH!*

The classroom door is KICKED entirely off its hinges. It flies through the air and slams into the front row of desks with deafening force. 

The music is drowned out by the screams of the students. They jump out of their seats. 

Na Hwa-jin stands in the doorway, his foot still raised. He surveys the room, his eyes lingering on the cowering Jin-woo, then locking onto Do-jin. He slowly walks to the front of the room, his leather shoes clicking loudly against the linoleum. 

He turns to the blackboard, picks up a piece of chalk, and writes his name in large, aggressive strokes that bite into the slate: *NA HWA-JIN.*
])

#character("NA HWA-JIN")
#dialogue([
I am Inspector Na Hwa-jin of the Educational Rights Protection Bureau. As of this exact second, I am your homeroom teacher.
])

#action([
Do-jin recovers from his initial shock. He feels his reputation is on the line. He scoffs loudly, kicking a desk aside as he walks up to Hwa-jin.
])

#character("BAE DO-JIN")
#dialogue([
ERPB? Are you kidding me? You think kicking a door scares us, old man? You're still just a teacher. You can't touch us. The law says so.
])

#action([
Hwa-jin slowly turns around. He looks down at the arrogant teenager.
])

#character("NA HWA-JIN")
#dialogue([
You're right. The Anti-Corporal Punishment Law, Article 31, Section 8. "No educator shall inflict physical pain upon a student for disciplinary purposes." It's a good law. It was made to protect innocent children.
])

#character("BAE DO-JIN")
#parenthetical("smirking, looking back at his friends")
#dialogue([
So back the hell off before I report you for even breathing on me. Go fetch me a coffee, teach.
])

#action([
Hwa-jin leans in until his face is inches from Do-jin's. His eyes are pitch black, terrifying.
])

#character("NA HWA-JIN")
#parenthetical("whispering dangerously")
#dialogue([
But you see, under the new Special Act on Educational Rights Protection, Article 1... ERPB inspectors are granted the authority to use *any means necessary* to restore order when a student is deemed a physical threat to the educational environment.
])

#action([
Do-jin frowns, confused. His smirk falters.
])

#character("BAE DO-JIN")
#dialogue([
What the hell does that mean?
])

#character("NA HWA-JIN")
#dialogue([
It means... you are no longer a student to me. And you are no longer protected.
])

#action([
Faster than the eye can track, Hwa-jin's hand shoots out. He grabs Do-jin by the collar of his expensive uniform, lifts the 180-pound teenager completely off the floor with one arm, and SLAMS him down onto the teacher's podium. 

The wood cracks loudly under the force. 

The entire class screams in pure, unadulterated shock. Several students scramble backward, pulling out their phones to record. 

Hwa-jin doesn't try to hide. He looks directly into the camera lenses.
])

#character("NA HWA-JIN")
#parenthetical("roaring")
#dialogue([
Record it! Send it to your parents! Send it to the police! Send it to the Blue House! Let everyone in this rotten country know that the rules have changed!
])

#action([
Hwa-jin pulls Do-jin up by his hair. The boy's nose is bleeding. His eyes are wide with genuine, unprecedented terror. Do-jin has never experienced physical violence directed at *him* before. He doesn't know how to process it. He is hyperventilating.
])

#character("BAE DO-JIN")
#parenthetical("sobbing, voice cracking")
#dialogue([
My dad... my dad is going to kill you! He'll sue you into the ground! You're dead!
])

#character("NA HWA-JIN")
#parenthetical("cold, deadpan")
#dialogue([
Tell him to get in line. 
])

#action([
Hwa-jin casually drops Do-jin onto the floor. Do-jin scrambles backward like a frightened crab until he hits the wall, trembling uncontrollably. 

Hwa-jin pulls a wet wipe from his pocket, methodically cleans his hands, and tosses the used wipe onto Do-jin's chest.
])

#character("NA HWA-JIN")
#dialogue([
Get back to your seat. Then turn to page one of your textbooks. Anyone whose eyes aren't on the page in five seconds is getting a personal lesson from me.
])

#action([
There is a flurry of frantic, terrified movement. Chairs scrape loudly against the floor. Books are slammed open. The classroom is perfectly, utterly silent, save for the sound of Do-jin quietly whimpering in the corner.

Hwa-jin stands at the podium. He straightens his tie. He looks out over the class. The reign of the bullies is over. 
])

#scene("INT. PRINCIPAL'S OFFICE - LATER THAT DAY")
#action([
The PRINCIPAL is hyperventilating, his face purple with rage. He is on the phone, looking through the glass blinds at Hwa-jin, who is sitting calmly on the office's expensive leather sofa, drinking the Principal's premium tea.
])

#character("PRINCIPAL")
#parenthetical("into the phone, sweating")
#dialogue([
Yes, Chairman Bae, I understand completely... Yes, it's an outrage! I will have him removed and arrested immediately! I promise you!
])

#action([
The Principal slams the phone down and glares at Hwa-jin.
])

#character("PRINCIPAL")
#dialogue([
Do you have any idea what you've done?! Bae Do-jin's father is the biggest donor to this foundation! He is pressing charges for aggravated assault! You're fired! I want you out of my school before the police get here!
])

#action([
Hwa-jin takes a slow, deliberate sip of his tea. He places the cup down, reaches into his inner jacket pocket, and pulls out a thick manila envelope. He tosses it onto the Principal's desk. Photographs spill out.
])

#character("NA HWA-JIN")
#dialogue([
Under the ERPB mandate, I have the authority to suspend any school official found complicit in the degradation of educational rights. 
])

#action([
The Principal looks at the photos. They show him accepting envelopes of cash from Chairman Bae at a luxury golf course.
])

#character("NA HWA-JIN")
#dialogue([
I've seen your offshore bank statements, Principal. I know exactly how much Bae's father pays you to ignore his son's extortion ring. I've already forwarded these files to the Supreme Prosecutor's Office.
])

#action([
The Principal freezes. All the color drains from his face. His knees give out, and he collapses into his chair.
])

#character("NA HWA-JIN")
#dialogue([
I'm not leaving. I'm just getting started. And if you get in my way, you won't just lose your pension... you'll die in prison. Cancel all your appointments. You work for me now.
])

#action([
Hwa-jin stands up, buttons his suit jacket, and walks out of the office, leaving the Principal utterly paralyzed.
])

#scene("EXT. JINWON HIGH SCHOOL - ROOFTOP - SUNSET")
#action([
Hwa-jin stands alone on the roof, the wind whipping his tie over his shoulder. He looks out over the sprawling city, the setting sun casting long, dark shadows over the school grounds. 

His phone buzzes. He answers it.
])

#character("IM HAN-RIM (V.O.)")
#parenthetical("sounding gleeful over the phone")
#dialogue([
The video of you throwing Do-jin hit ten million views in three hours, Boss. The internet is having a meltdown. The human rights groups are calling for your head, but the parents' associations are cheering in the streets. Phase One is complete.
])

#character("NA HWA-JIN")
#dialogue([
Good. Let them scream. Prepare the dossiers for the rest of the faculty here. 
])

#action([
Hwa-jin looks down at the courtyard below. The final bell has rung. 

For the first time in years, the students are walking out of the gates quietly. Orderly. No fights. No screams. Jin-woo walks out, clutching his backpack, looking around in disbelief that he wasn't jumped. 

The students cast fearful glances up toward the third-floor windows. They are terrified. But it's a fear that brings peace.
])

#character("NA HWA-JIN")
#dialogue([
If we want to clean this school up permanently, breaking the bullies isn't enough. Tomorrow, we fix the teachers who forgot how to fight back. 
])

#action([
Hwa-jin hangs up the phone. He turns and walks back toward the stairwell, his silhouette fading into the shadows.

FADE OUT.
])